# Gate step 1470-v67y — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS. The operator ruled (2026-09-17, 1247-amcu) that every refusal
# says why it refused and what would make it not a refusal; a bare verdict
# token leaves an agent stuck with no next action. build.sh --check runs
# scripts/lua/check-refusal-affordance-added.lua, which refuses an ADDED
# refused:/blocked:/violation: emission with no why/remedy (or _afford, or a
# reasoned affordance-ok marker) nearby; --audit counts coverage per site. The
# fixture drives the guard over scratch repos, and checks the audit per site.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking a newly-added refusal cannot ship without its affordance (1470-v67y)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-refusal-affordance-added.sh"
STEP_ERROR="the refusal-affordance guard no longer refuses a bare added verdict, or its audit stopped counting per site (1470-v67y); see which arm failed above"
STEP_OK="newly-added refusals carry why and remedy; audit counts per site"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="tlatoanis-macbook-air 2026-09-28 darwin ok:refusal-affordance-added-fixture:8/8"
# ORDER 2155-gpar: runs alone, never beside a sibling step in the gate pool.
STEP_SERIAL="writes fixed-name scratch or mutant files inside the checkout"
STEP_LANES="checkout"
# ORDER 2157-ginp: STEP_READS, the paths this step reads, RECORDED ONLY: never
# consulted by the class-selector skip (that is STEP_INPUTS, 2118-tnut). First
# cut: the step's own script plus every repo path it names literally.
STEP_READS="scripts/lua/check-refusal-affordance-added.lua scripts/test-refusal-affordance-added.sh"
